# Shell scripts run inside the Linux dev container from this Windows working
# tree, and bash cannot read a CRLF shebang. core.autocrlf would otherwise
# write them out with CRLF on checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The git hooks are shell scripts without the extension, so the rule above does
# not reach them. A CRLF hook is worse than a broken one: sh carries the \r into
# the command it runs, and `npx lint-staged` fails as `undefined@lint-staged`
# rather than as a lint failure.
.husky/* text eol=lf
